ú
Definitions

Design Revision    Defines an optional combination of up to 59
                   alphanumeric characters used to designate the
                   current version of the design.


                   ş    You can use other symbols or punctuation;
                        however you cannot use the dollar sign, $.

                   ş    You can use reserved words in this statement.

ú
Use
The following error conditions pertain to the REVISION statement.

ş    Without the REVISION statement, the software issues a warning and
     continues processing the file.

ş    With multiple REVISION statements, the software issues an error
     and stops processing the file.
